00:27:53.287 --> 00:27:55.370
A couple of different
discounts that are available

00:27:55.370 --> 00:27:58.430
primarily for
Compute Engine, those

00:27:58.430 --> 00:28:02.186
are both sustained and
committed use discounts.

00:28:02.186 --> 00:28:04.310
They're both cool, so we
want to make sure that you

00:28:04.310 --> 00:28:05.840
save as much money as possible.

00:28:05.840 --> 00:28:07.160
Customers tend to like that.

00:28:07.160 --> 00:28:09.480
So sustained discounts is
pretty straightforward.

00:28:09.480 --> 00:28:13.190
If you're using a virtual
machine or virtual machines

00:28:13.190 --> 00:28:15.020
and you use them over
a period of time,

00:28:15.020 --> 00:28:16.970
Google will
specifically give you

00:28:16.970 --> 00:28:20.600
a discount of up to 30%
net for instances that

00:28:20.600 --> 00:28:21.950
run up to the entire month.

00:28:21.950 --> 00:28:24.600
And there's sort of a sliding
scale on that as well.

00:28:24.600 --> 00:28:25.580
So you really don't
have to do anything,

00:28:25.580 --> 00:28:26.330
which is kind of cool.

00:28:26.330 --> 00:28:27.440
You just use what you use.

00:28:27.440 --> 00:28:29.940
And the more you use it, the
more of a discount we give you.

00:28:29.940 --> 00:28:33.466
What's nice as well though is,
if you're maybe a little less

00:28:33.466 --> 00:28:35.840
elastic in your load, or you've
been doing it for a while

00:28:35.840 --> 00:28:39.200
and you know what
sort of memory and CPU

00:28:39.200 --> 00:28:41.290
that you use over
a period of time,

00:28:41.290 --> 00:28:44.270
say a year or three years which
is what we're talking about,

00:28:44.270 --> 00:28:46.970
you can actually sign up for
a committed used discount.

00:28:46.970 --> 00:28:49.260
So this is where
you're actually saying,

00:28:49.260 --> 00:28:51.230
OK, I'm going to
agree that I will

00:28:51.230 --> 00:28:53.930
use this much CPU and this
much memory over a year

00:28:53.930 --> 00:28:55.520
or two years or
three years, and then

00:28:55.520 --> 00:28:57.060
you can purchase that up front.

00:28:57.060 --> 00:28:58.790
And if you do that,
you can get up

00:28:58.790 --> 00:29:01.940
to a 57% discount off
normal prices in return

00:29:01.940 --> 00:29:03.590
